@title Consumer lag alert runbook
@subtitle Streaming team, Corvid Payments: settlement-consumer on payments-events

## Alert thresholds

table = Severity,Lag (messages),Duration,Action; Warning,50000,10 minutes,Slack only; Critical,250000,5 minutes,page on-call; Emergency,1000000,any,page on-call and the Streaming lead

## Triage flow

diagram triage title="Consumer lag triage"

triage: alert "Lag alert fires"
triage: run "Consumers running?"
triage: restart "Restart consumers"
triage: skew "Partition skew?"
triage: rebal "Rebalance partitions"
triage: scale "Scale out consumers"
triage: rec "Lag recovering"
triage: alert -> run
triage: run -> restart : no
triage: run -> skew : yes
triage: skew -> rebal : yes
triage: skew -> scale : no
triage: restart -> rec
triage: rebal -> rec
triage: scale -> rec

## Steps

1. Check the consumer pods in the streaming namespace.
2. Check per-partition lag.
3. If one partition holds more than 40% of the lag, treat it as skew.
4. Scale the deployment to at most 24 replicas, because the topic has 24 partitions.

!!! Never reset consumer offsets to latest. Unprocessed settlements would be skipped and would have to be reconciled by hand.

! If lag is still growing after 30 minutes, escalate to the Streaming lead.
